#: ../../../contributing.md:3
msgid "Contributing to the libc Project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:5
msgid ""
"LLVM-libc is being developed as part of the LLVM project so contributions to "
"the libc project should also follow the general LLVM [contribution "
"guidelines](https://llvm.org/docs/Contributing.html). Below is a list of "
"open projects that one can start with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:10
msgid ""
"**Beginner Bugs** - Help us tackle [good first issues](https://github.com/"
"llvm/llvm-project/issues?"
"q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3Alibc+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22). These "
"bugs have been tagged with the github labels \"libc\" and \"good first "
"issue\" by the team as potentially easier places to get started. Please do "
"first check if the bug has an assignee; if so please find another unless "
"there's been no movement on the issue from the assignee, in which place do "
"ask if you can help take over. Remember to follow the LLVM [AI Tool Use "
"Policy](https://llvm.org/docs/AIToolPolicy.html) which forbids using LLMs "
"for good first issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:19
msgid ""
"**Cleanup code-style** - The libc project follows the general [LLVM style]"
"(https://llvm.org/docs/CodingStandards.html) with specific conventions for "
"naming (`snake_case` for functions, `CamelCase` for types). See the {doc}"
"`code style <dev/code_style>` page for the authoritative reference. "
"Mechanical projects to move parts following old styles to the current "
"conventions are welcome."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:26
msgid ""
"**Implement Linux syscall wrappers** - A large portion of the POSIX API can "
"be implemented as syscall wrappers on Linux. A good number have already been "
"implemented but many more are yet to be implemented. So, a project of medium "
"complexity would be to implement syscall wrappers which have not yet been "
"implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:31
msgid ""
"**Update the clang-tidy lint rules and use them in the build and/or CI** - "
"The libc project has a set of clang-tidy checks (see {ref}`clang-tidy checks "
"<clang_tidy_checks>`) but they are not enabled by default. They can be "
"enabled by configuring with `-DLLVM_LIBC_ENABLE_LINTING=ON` (or by setting "
"`LLVM_LIBC_CLANG_TIDY`) and running the `libc-lint` build target. This "
"project is about keeping the checks up to date and reintegrating them into "
"the build and CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:38
msgid ""
"**double and higher precision math functions** - These are under active "
"development but you can take a shot at those not yet implemented. See {ref}"
"`math` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:41
msgid ""
"**Contribute a new OS/Architecture port** - You can contribute a new "
"operating system or target architecture port. See {ref}`porting` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:45
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:47
msgid ""
"Read {ref}`design_philosophy` and {ref}`abi_policy` to understand what the "
"project is and is not trying to do. Read {ref}`implementation_guidelines` "
"for how code is expected to be written, and {ref}`patterns_to_avoid` before "
"modelling new code on something that is already in the tree, because older "
"code does not always follow the current conventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:53
msgid ""
"Some changes are worth discussing with the maintainers before investing in "
"an implementation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:56
msgid ""
"a non-trivial change to the layout of an existing public type or the value "
"of an existing public macro, or exporting a symbol under a name other than "
"its standard one (see {ref}`abi_policy`),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:59
msgid "a function that is not in the C or POSIX standards,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:60
msgid "a new configuration option,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:61
msgid "new code under `libc/shared/`, or a new user of it,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:62
msgid "any code written in assembly (see {ref}`assembly_policy`),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:63
msgid "any intentional deviation from a standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:65
msgid ""
"The easiest way to reach out is to ask in the `#libc` channel on the [LLVM "
"Discord](https://discord.gg/xS7Z362)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:68
msgid "Pull requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:70
msgid ""
"**Keep pull requests small and focused.** Add one function, or one closely "
"related family of functions, per pull request. Land refactoring separately "
"from the change that needs it. A bug found along the way gets its own pull "
"request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:74
msgid ""
"**Title.** Start the title with `[libc]`, and add a second tag where one "
"applies: `[libc][math]`, `[libc][docs]`, or `[libc][NFC]` for changes with "
"no functional effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:77
msgid ""
"**Format the change.** Run `clang-format` on C++ sources and `libc/utils/"
"cmake_format.py -i` on the CMake files you edited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:79
msgid ""
"**Test in both build modes** where the code supports both. See {ref}"
"`testing_guide`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:81
msgid ""
"**Do not mention people with `@` in commit messages**, or in a pull request "
"description that will become one. GitHub notifies them again each time the "
"commit is pushed to another fork. Request reviews through the reviewers "
"field instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:85
msgid ""
"**Bazel.** Updating the Bazel build files is not required, but it is "
"appreciated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:88
msgid ""
"LLVM-libc follows LLVM's [patch reversion policy](https://llvm.org/docs/"
"DeveloperPolicy.html#patch-reversion-policy). A change that breaks a "
"buildbot is reverted or, if the fix is trivial, fixed forward. When "
"relanding, describe what went wrong and how it was fixed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:93
msgid "AI-assisted contributions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:95
msgid ""
"LLVM's [AI Tool Use Policy](https://llvm.org/docs/AIToolPolicy.html) applies "
"to LLVM-libc. Read it before using AI tools on a contribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:98
msgid "Tools make some mistakes in this project more often than people do:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:100
msgid ""
"They imitate the code around them, including code that follows outdated "
"conventions. See {ref}`patterns_to_avoid`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:102
msgid ""
"Asked to make a program work, they change LLVM-libc's types, symbols, or "
"behavior to match another libc, because that is the shortest path to a "
"passing build. See {ref}`making_existing_software_work`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:105
msgid ""
"They reproduce code from other C libraries. That is not allowed, regardless "
"of how the code was produced. See {ref}`original_implementations`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:107
msgid ""
"They call one public function from another. See {ref}"
"`entrypoints_do_not_call_entrypoints`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:110
msgid "Check for these before asking for review."
msgstr ""
